import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Data workshop notes" description="Stack, cost, engines, and the positioning sources. Prices and dates were checked 27 Nov 2026 in the positioning notes.">
  <article class="wrap band">
    <p class="kicker">From the workshop design and the positioning notes</p>
    <h1>Notes</h1>
    <h2>Why dbt v1 is the main lane</h2>
    <p>Local MetricFlow (dbt-metricflow 0.16.0 in the design) requires dbt-core 1.11 or 1.12. The design names dbt-core 1.12.7 and dbt-duckdb 1.11.1 as the main lane, and dbt v2 as a portability lane. The starter does not install dbt in the default setup command. The project files are there for <code>dbt deps</code> when you want them.</p>
    <h2>Medallion, mapped to dbt</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Home</th><th>Naming</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Loader, declared as sources</td><td>bronze.&lt;system&gt;__&lt;entity&gt;</td><td>Append-only. Never updated.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Silver, clean</td><td>models/staging</td><td>stg_&lt;system&gt;__&lt;entity&gt;</td><td>1:1 with the source. Rename, cast, dedupe. PII hashed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Silver, history</td><td>snapshots and intermediate</td><td>snap_, int_</td><td>SCD2, business rules, conflicts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gold</td><td>models/marts</td><td>dim_, fct_, mart_</td><td>Documented, versioned, exposures</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Semantic</td><td>YAML on gold</td><td>metric names</td><td>Defined once. Queried by agents.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2>Semantic layer options, as recorded 26 Nov 2026</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Cost in the design</th><th>Local DuckDB</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>MetricFlow mf</td><td>$0</td><td>Yes. Your MCP server is D6.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>dbt Semantic Layer on the platform</td><td>Starter $100/user/month in the design. Not in the free Developer plan.</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cube Core</td><td>$0 self-hosted</td><td>Yes, DuckDB driver</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Boring Semantic Layer</td><td>$0</td><td>Yes, via Ibis</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h2>Cost</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Default path: everything local on DuckDB. D6 on Ollama, or Workers AI's free allowance for small runs. $0.</li>
      <li>Optional MotherDuck Lite and R2 free tiers. $0 in the design.</li>
      <li>D9: Elementary OSS, Dagster OSS, a webhook sink. $0.</li>
      <li>Hosted Dagster+ Solo after the trial: $10/month plus usage, in the design.</li>
      <li>Hosted dbt Semantic Layer: $100/user/month (Starter), in the design, and not on DuckDB.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Still open in the design</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Public monorepo with a solutions branch, or private? This repo is the public-starter shape: solutions are not on main.</li>
      <li>Dagster everywhere, or only in D9? This repo teaches Dagster in D9 and leaves cron as the fallback.</li>
      <li>D6 agent language. The metrics server stub is Python, because MetricFlow is Python. The context harness can still drive a TypeScript agent.</li>
      <li>Whether the main lane moves to dbt v2 once local MetricFlow supports it.</li>
    </ul>
